ivcrtest includes code adapted from the UnionBounds R package by
Xinyue Bei, https://github.com/xinyuebei-econ/UnionBounds, which
accompanies

  Bei, X. (2024). Inference on union bounds. SSRN Working Paper 5023605.
  https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.5023605

The adapted functions are:

  R/CIhybrid.R        CIhybrid(), adapted from CI_ModifiedConditional()
  R/CIcon.R           CIcon()
  R/CIcon_TNbounds.R  CIcon_TNbounds()
  R/CIproj_p.R        CIproj_p()

The ivcrtest versions take a user-supplied map g, so that the grid-level
bounds may be nonlinear in the estimated parameters. They also use
stats::optim() in place of nloptr, take an explicit seed, and differ in
their arguments and return values.

